_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ%For I have kept the ways of the LORD,¦layout ‚¤textÙ+And have not wickedly departed from my God.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ%For all his judgments were before me:¦layout ‚¤textÙ4And as for his statutes, I did not depart from them.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤text¾I was also upright before him,¦layout ‚¤textÙ(And have kept myself from mine iniquity.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙETherefore the LORD hath recompensed me according to my righteousness;¦layout ‚¤textÙ+According to my cleanness in his eye sight.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ2With the merciful thou wilt shew thyself merciful,¦layout ‚¤textÙ8And with the upright man thou wilt shew thyself upright.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ*With the pure thou wilt shew thyself pure;¦layout ‚¤textÙ6And with the froward thou wilt shew thyself unsavoury.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ(And the afflicted people thou wilt save:¦layout ‚¤textÙFBut thine eyes are upon the haughty, that thou mayest bring them down.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse…¤book	§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse%¦verses™„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤text½For thou art my lamp, O LORD:¦layout ‚¤textÙ&And the LORD will lighten my darkness.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ'For by thee I have run through a troop:¦layout ‚¤textÙ$By my God have I leaped over a wall.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines“‚¤text¿As for God, his way is perfect;¦layout ‚¤text¾The word of the LORD is tried:¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ.He is a buckler to all them that trust in him.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤text¾For who is God, save the LORD?¦layout ‚¤textÙ And who is a rock, save our God?¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤text½God is my strength and power:¦layout ‚¤text½And he maketh my way perfect.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ#He maketh my feet like hinds' feet:¦layout ‚¤textÙ#And setteth me upon my high places.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤text¼He teacheth my hands to war;¦layout ‚¤textÙ.So that a bow of steel is broken by mine arms.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ4Thou hast also given me the shield of thy salvation:¦layout ‚¤textÙ&And thy gentleness hath made me great.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ%Thou hast enlarged my steps under me;¦layout ‚¤text½So that my feet did not slip.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse%…¤book	§chapter«first_verse&ªlast_verse.¦verses™„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ0I have pursued mine enemies, and destroyed them;¦layout ‚¤textÙ/And turned not again until I had consumed them.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙFAnd I have consumed them, and wounded them, that they could not arise:¦layout ‚¤textÙ#Yea, they are fallen under my feet.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ0For thou hast girded me with strength to battle:¦layout ‚¤textÙ8Them that rose up against me hast thou subdued under me.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse(„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ2Thou hast also given me the necks of mine enemies,¦layout ‚¤textÙ'That I might destroy them that hate me.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse)„¥verse*¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ(They looked, but there was none to save;¦layout ‚¤textÙ-Even unto the LORD, but he answered them not.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse*„¥verse+¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ7Then did I beat them as small as the dust of the earth,¦layout ‚¤textÙGI did stamp them as the mire of the street, and did spread them abroad.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse+„¥verse,¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines“‚¤textÙ<Thou also hast delivered me from the strivings of my people,¦layout ‚¤textÙ,Thou hast kept me to be head of the heathen:¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ)A people which I knew not shall serve me.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse,„¥verse-¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ*Strangers shall submit themselves unto me:¦layout ‚¤textÙ5As soon as they hear, they shall be obedient unto me.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse-„¥verse.¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textºStrangers shall fade away,¦layout ‚¤textÙ3And they shall be afraid out of their close places.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse.…¤book	§chapter«first_verse/ªlast_verse3¦verses•„¥verse/¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ(The LORD liveth; and blessed be my rock;¦layout ‚¤textÙ3And exalted be the God of the rock of my salvation.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse/„¥verse0¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤text»It is God that avengeth me,¦layout ‚¤textÙ+And that bringeth down the people under me,¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse0„¥verse1¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines“‚¤textÙ-And that bringeth me forth from mine enemies:¦layout ‚¤textÙGThou also hast lifted me up on high above them that rose up against me:¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ,Thou hast delivered me from the violent man.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse1„¥verse2¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙBTherefore I will give thanks unto thee, O LORD, among the heathen,¦layout ‚¤textÙ&And I will sing praises unto thy name.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse2„¥verse3¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines“‚¤textÙ*He is the tower of salvation for his king:¦layout ‚¤textÙ"And sheweth mercy to his anointed,¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ)Unto David, and to his seed for evermore.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse3